 "title": "The Barrow Roads",
 "kind": "war",
 "seed": 4202,
 "max_tier": 3,
 "ai": "easy",
 "intro": [
  "Every barrow along the south road has opened. The dead march north in columns, too orderly for corpses. Maelis Thorne has tracked them to a single grave-town in the marsh, Mournfield, kept by a gravedigger who buried half of them himself: Sexton Grue.",
  "How to play: this is a war chapter. Greyhold builds and recruits as in a skirmish: your workers gather, dwellings raise soldiers, and you can raise troops up to tier 3 here. Take the villages on the way for their workers and gold.",
  "While a barrow on the south road stands open it sends a column of dead north to Greyhold every minute and a half. Burn the three barrows, then take Mournfield. If Greyhold and every village you hold fall, the chapter is lost."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "if": {
    "flag": "learned_corvin"
   },
   "text": [
    "Mournfield burns, and the columns stop. But the dead in its pits were not all Greyhold's: some wore the grey of the fen villages further south, where the lantern temples stand.",
    "Grue's last words were a name. Father Corvin Mire, a lantern-priest of the fen, who taught a gravedigger how to make the dead walk in rows."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": [
    "Mournfield burns, and the columns stop. But the dead in its pits were not all Greyhold's: some wore the grey of the fen villages further south, where the lantern temples stand.",
    "Whatever taught Sexton Grue to raise them came from the fens. The road goes south."
   ]
  }
